mkv-extractor-qt6 (@VERSION@) unstable; urgency=medium

  Unofficial build from the fork at https://github.com/mskpluk/MKV-Extractor-Qt6

  * Extracting an audio track with no name works again. Execute used to do
    nothing at all on most releases, which carry a single unnamed track.
  * Remux works again: every path through it died on a missing import.
  * Remux no longer writes the table placeholder as the track name, and the
    video track keeps its language.
  * Extracted files are named after the language of the track, and an
    extracted video gets the extension of its codec instead of .mkv.
  * The program has its icon back in the menu.
  * The About entry and six translations no longer call this Qt5.
  * The package depends on the PySide6 packages that actually exist, so it
    installs on Debian and Ubuntu.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  @DATE@
